  "body": "Notably, this renames \"canonical case\" to \"canonical keyword\", and\ndefines exactly how it is used. Closes #3685.\n\nThis also rearranges the CORS settings attribute definition a bit to\nmatch other enumerated attributes more closely.\n\n---\n\nI would have liked to put the No CORS state into the table as well, but I couldn't figure out what to put in the keywords column that would avoid confusion. (Since it has no keywords.)\n\nThe reflection \"algorithm\" got kind of messy, but I didn't want to try to overhaul that into an actual algorithm with steps at this point, so hopefully it's OK.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5378/common-dom-interfaces.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 19, 2020, 9:30 PM UTC (a4c7854)\">/common-dom-interfaces.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5378/2053069...a4c7854/common-dom-interfaces.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 19, 2020, 9:30 PM UTC (a4c7854)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5378/urls-and-fetching.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 19, 2020, 9:30 PM UTC (a4c7854)\">/urls-and-fetching.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5378/2053069...a4c7854/urls-and-fetching.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 19, 2020, 9:30 PM UTC (a4c7854)\">diff</a> )",
